{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792580640073,"sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","part":{"partID":"prt_15e21dbd7002RmajhcusMVr9M1","sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","messageID":"msg_15e21d005001D0W4ywV9mdrnOc","type":"tool","id":"call_0c7bdfadf740429d8a3b78b1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/VIEW_LICENSE_PATH.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/VIEW_LICENSE_PATH.md, lines 1-1\n1: LICENSE","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/VIEW_LICENSE_PATH.md, lines 1-1\n1: LICENSE"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/VIEW_LICENSE_PATH.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792580639703,"end":1792580640073}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792580640074,"sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","part":{"partID":"prt_15e21dbdc0011eibPC9fIC9ekg","sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","messageID":"msg_15e21d005001D0W4ywV9mdrnOc","type":"tool","id":"call_2ec664a04a134ce2adc16c88","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md, lines 1-69\n1: # Personal Project Board - local single-user kanban board\n2: \n3: ## What this is\n4: A dependency-free (Python 3 standard library only) local web app for one person: named\n5: boards, user-named ordered columns, cards with a title and a short description, and card\n6: movement between columns and inside a column. A card's column IS its status - there is no\n7: separate status field. Everything is stored in one SQLite file inside a data directory you\n8: choose, so boards, columns, card order and card positions survive a restart.\n9: \n10: ## Requirements\n11: - Python 3.9 or newer, standard library only (http.server, sqlite3, json, urllib.parse)\n12: - no third-party packages, no network access\n13: \n14: ## Layout\n15:     app.py            entry point (argument parsing, server wiring)\n16:     personal_board/   db.py, service.py, api.py, web.py, server.py\n17:     probe.py          acceptance probe (stdlib only)\n18:     README.md         this file\n19:     data/             default data directory, created on first run\n20: \n21: ## Start the app\n22:     python3 app.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765 --data-dir ./data\n23:     # the default data directory can also be set with PERSONAL_KANBAN_DATA_DIR=./data\n24: \n25: Then open http://127.0.0.1:8765/ in a browser. The JSON API lives under\n26: http://127.0.0.1:8765/api/ (health check: GET /api/health).\n27: \n28: Stop the process with Ctrl-C. Start it again with the same --data-dir: the boards, the\n29: column order, the card order and the per-column counts are read back unchanged from\n30: <data-dir>/kanban.sqlite3.\n31: \n32: ## Run the acceptance probe\n33: Start the app first, then:\n34:     python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case A01\n35:     python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case all\n36: \n37: Cases (one per feature):\n38:     A01  boards: create, list, read, rename, delete + 7 rejected writes\n39:     A02  columns: seed, add, rename, reorder, delete guards\n40:     A03  cards: create, read, edit + 12 rejected writes\n41:     A04  movement: cross-column move, in-column reorder, rejected moves\n42:     A05  read model: exact counts and sets, stable second read, date edges\n43: \n44: Exit code 0 means every selected case passed, 1 means at least one case failed. Each case\n45: creates its own disposable board and deletes only the records it created; no pre-existing\n46: data is ever deleted, so run the probe against a scratch data directory.\n47: \n48: ## Manual restart check (operator step, not executed by the probe)\n49: 1. Start the app with a scratch data directory, create one board with three columns and\n50:    two cards, and note GET /api/boards/{id}.\n51: 2. Stop the process (Ctrl-C) and start it again with the same --data-dir.\n52: 3. GET /api/boards and GET /api/boards/{id}: the board, the column order, the card order\n53:    and the per-column card_count must be identical to step 1.\n54: \n55: The probe cannot stop or start the server, so it does not and does not claim to verify\n56: this step.\n57: \n58: ## Verification status\n59: Runtime verification of this blueprint: not_run. No server was started, no request was\n60: issued and no probe case was executed while this document was written; the acceptance\n61: criteria describe what must hold, not what was observed. The upstream project (Kanboard)\n62: was read as a pinned design reference only: it was neither installed nor run, and no\n63: upstream source was copied into the target.\n64: \n65: ## Out of scope for P0\n66: Accounts and login, roles and permissions, multi-user collaboration, a separate status\n67: field, WIP limits, swimlanes, due/start dates and recurrence, notifications, time\n68: tracking and reports, automation, templates, search and filtering, archive, secondary\n69: views, external integrations.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md, lines 1-69\n1: # Personal Project Board - local single-user kanban board\n2: \n3: ## What this is\n4: A dependency-free (Python 3 standard library only) local web app for one person: named\n5: boards, user-named ordered columns, cards with a title and a short description, and card\n6: movement between columns and inside a column. A card's column IS its status - there is no\n7: separate status field. Everything is stored in one SQLite file inside a data directory you\n8: choose, so boards, columns, card order and card positions survive a restart.\n9: \n10: ## Requirements\n11: - Python 3.9 or newer, standard library only (http.server, sqlite3, json, urllib.parse)\n12: - no third-party packages, no network access\n13: \n14: ## Layout\n15:     app.py            entry point (argument parsing, server wiring)\n16:     personal_board/   db.py, service.py, api.py, web.py, server.py\n17:     probe.py          acceptance probe (stdlib only)\n18:     README.md         this file\n19:     data/             default data directory, created on first run\n20: \n21: ## Start the app\n22:     python3 app.py --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765 --data-dir ./data\n23:     # the default data directory can also be set with PERSONAL_KANBAN_DATA_DIR=./data\n24: \n25: Then open http://127.0.0.1:8765/ in a browser. The JSON API lives under\n26: http://127.0.0.1:8765/api/ (health check: GET /api/health).\n27: \n28: Stop the process with Ctrl-C. Start it again with the same --data-dir: the boards, the\n29: column order, the card order and the per-column counts are read back unchanged from\n30: <data-dir>/kanban.sqlite3.\n31: \n32: ## Run the acceptance probe\n33: Start the app first, then:\n34:     python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case A01\n35:     python3 probe.py --base-url http://127.0.0.1:8765 --case all\n36: \n37: Cases (one per feature):\n38:     A01  boards: create, list, read, rename, delete + 7 rejected writes\n39:     A02  columns: seed, add, rename, reorder, delete guards\n40:     A03  cards: create, read, edit + 12 rejected writes\n41:     A04  movement: cross-column move, in-column reorder, rejected moves\n42:     A05  read model: exact counts and sets, stable second read, date edges\n43: \n44: Exit code 0 means every selected case passed, 1 means at least one case failed. Each case\n45: creates its own disposable board and deletes only the records it created; no pre-existing\n46: data is ever deleted, so run the probe against a scratch data directory.\n47: \n48: ## Manual restart check (operator step, not executed by the probe)\n49: 1. Start the app with a scratch data directory, create one board with three columns and\n50:    two cards, and note GET /api/boards/{id}.\n51: 2. Stop the process (Ctrl-C) and start it again with the same --data-dir.\n52: 3. GET /api/boards and GET /api/boards/{id}: the board, the column order, the card order\n53:    and the per-column card_count must be identical to step 1.\n54: \n55: The probe cannot stop or start the server, so it does not and does not claim to verify\n56: this step.\n57: \n58: ## Verification status\n59: Runtime verification of this blueprint: not_run. No server was started, no request was\n60: issued and no probe case was executed while this document was written; the acceptance\n61: criteria describe what must hold, not what was observed. The upstream project (Kanboard)\n62: was read as a pinned design reference only: it was neither installed nor run, and no\n63: upstream source was copied into the target.\n64: \n65: ## Out of scope for P0\n66: Accounts and login, roles and permissions, multi-user collaboration, a separate status\n67: field, WIP limits, swimlanes, due/start dates and recurrence, notifications, time\n68: tracking and reports, automation, templates, search and filtering, archive, secondary\n69: views, external integrations."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/acceptance/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792580639708,"end":1792580640074}}}}
