{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792580645879,"sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","part":{"partID":"prt_15e21f3d6001xgd5Z4PqNjFItJ","sessionID":"ses_ea1de83daffetTStmPb5FvGcdC","messageID":"msg_15e21e694001B6iSJlKwJpsmij","type":"tool","id":"call_1c1432f2501b4f31afe871ae","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-minimax-batch-2026-10-21/personal-kanban/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md, lines 1-34\n1: Kanboard\n2: ========\n3: \n4: Kanboard is project management software that focuses on the Kanban methodology.\n5: \n6: **This application is in maintenance mode**. What does it mean?\n7: \n8: Citing [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maintenance_mode):\n9: \n10: > In the world of software development, maintenance mode refers to a point in a computer program's life when it has reached all of its goals and is generally considered to be \"complete\" and bug-free. The term can also refer to the point in a software product's evolution when it is no longer competitive with other products or current with regard to the technology environment it operates within.\n11: \n12: - The [author](#credits) of this application is not actively developing any new major features (only small fixes)\n13: - New releases are published regularly depending on the contributions made by the community\n14: - Pull requests for new features and bug fixes are accepted as long as the [guidelines](.github/pull_request_template.md) are followed\n15: \n16: Table of Contents\n17: -----------------\n18: \n19: - Official website: <https://kanboard.org/>\n20: - [List of features](https://kanboard.org/#features)\n21: - [Change Log](https://github.com/kanboard/kanboard/blob/main/ChangeLog)\n22: - [Forum](